    ],
    "tips": [
      {
        "id": "like-ing",
        "title": "I like + -ing",
        "body": [
          "**Ku-** ya Kiswahili mara nyingi ni **to**: **kuimba → to sing**. Baada ya **like**, Kiingereza hupendelea **-ing**: **I like singing** (ninapenda kuimba).",
          "Vivyo hivyo: **I love dancing**, **She enjoys swimming**. Baada ya **want**, tumia **to**: **I want to swim.**"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "play-dance",
        "title": "Play au dance?",
        "body": [
          "**Kucheza** ina maneno mawili kwa Kiingereza: **play** kwa michezo (**play football**, **play cards**) na **dance** kwa densi.",
          "Muziki: **play the drums** (piga ngoma), **sing a song** (imba wimbo), **listen to music** (sikiliza muziki)."
        ]
      }
    ],
    "culture": [
      {
        "title": "Premier League",
        "body": [
          "Mashabiki wengi Afrika Mashariki hufuatilia **Premier League** ya Uingereza. Utasikia **What’s the score?** (matokeo ni ngapi?) na **It’s a draw** (sare)."
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
